# .gitignore — Turn 5 "App Starting Point" (Python / Django template)
#
# Ported from the Rails sister template's secret-protection patterns and
# adapted for a Python / Django / uv / Tailwind-CLI stack.
#
# The single most important job of this file is to make it IMPOSSIBLE to
# accidentally commit a secret. Future sessions are driven by non-technical
# execs; the path of least resistance must also be the safe one.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Python
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.so
.Python
build/
dist/
*.egg-info/
.eggs/
*.egg

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Tooling caches (pytest, ruff, mypy)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.dmypy.json
dmypy.json

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Test coverage (pytest-cov)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
htmlcov/
.coverage
.coverage.*
coverage.xml
*.cover

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# uv / virtualenv
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.venv/
env/
venv/
ENV/
# .python-version IS committed — it pins Python 3.13 for every fork created
#   from this template (uv reads it). Do not ignore it.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Django
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.log
local_settings.py
# SQLite prototype DB lives in db/ (see config/settings/dev.py). Ignore the
# data files but keep the directory tracked via db/.keep.
db/*.sqlite3
db/*.sqlite3-journal
db/*.sqlite3-[0-9]*
db/development.sqlite3
# Defensive: catch any stray root-level SQLite file too.
db.sqlite3
db.sqlite3-journal
# collectstatic output and user uploads (source assets live in static/, tracked).
staticfiles/
media/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Tailwind CLI binary cache + build output (django-tailwind-cli)
#   The standalone binary and auto-generated source live in .django_tailwind_cli/.
#   The compiled stylesheet is a build artifact rebuilt by `manage.py tailwind
#   build` (run from bin/setup); do not commit it.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.django_tailwind_cli/
static/css/tailwind.css

# django-migration-linter local analysis cache (CI runs with --no-cache).
*.pickle

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Environment / secrets — every depth, every common backup pattern
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.env
.env.*
**/.env
**/.env.*
.envrc
**/.envrc
# Editor / OS backups of env files (people open .env in Notepad / VS Code / Office)
.env~
.env.bak
.env.backup
.env.old
.env.swp
.env.swo
~$.env*
.env.tmp
# ...but DO track the secret-free template that documents the keys.
# (The .env.* glob above would otherwise swallow it — this negation re-includes it.)
!.env.example

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Private keys and certs of any kind, anywhere
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
*.crt
*.cer
*.der
id_rsa
id_dsa
id_ecdsa
id_ed25519
*.ppk

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Claude Code — per-user local settings may hold local grants; never commit.
# (.claude/settings.json IS tracked and shared; settings.local.json is not.)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.claude/settings.local.json

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# OS & editor cruft
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.idea/
# Ignore VS Code workspace files but allow a shared, committed settings.json.
# NOTE: we ignore .vscode/* (contents) rather than .vscode/ (the dir) so that
# git can actually re-include the negated file below — re-inclusion fails if
# the parent directory itself is excluded.
.vscode/*
!.vscode/settings.json
*.swp
*.swo
*~

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Decision artifacts
#   .env.example     — tracked (keys only, no secrets); re-included above.
#   setup_decisions.md — tracked when it exists (secret-free summary). It is
#       deliberately NOT created yet: its absence signals to a future Claude
#       that the first-run setup interview has not been done. It is intentionally
#       NOT listed as an ignore entry, so it commits normally once created.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
